{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467732-unbelief-integrating-aliens","id":1467732,"title":"Unbelief, integrating aliens","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-13T15:53:45-08:00","id":1467732,"title":"Unbelief, integrating aliens","content":"What are the mechanics of Unbelief? <br /> <br /> What is required to integrate into society a human-appearing creature that has alien DNA so they no longer face Rejection or from the Consensus or Pattern Bleed?<br /> <br /> Please bare with me. I may be using these terms improperly. M20 Core's index does not have an entry for Unbelief.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T18:07:43-08:00","id":1467744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467732-unbelief-integrating-aliens#post1467732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the mechanics of Unbelief? <br /> <br /> What is required to integrate into society a human-appearing creature that has alien DNA so they no longer face Rejection or from the Consensus or Pattern Bleed?<br /> <br /> Please bare with me. I may be using these terms improperly. M20 Core's index does not have an entry for Unbelief.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does their belief affect the consensus? Do they have serious supernatural backing? The answers affect the outcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T19:10:10-08:00","id":1467748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467732-unbelief-integrating-aliens?p=1467744#post1467744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does their belief affect the consensus? Do they have serious supernatural backing? The answers affect the outcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>While they have totally human appearance, the hair and skin cells they shed hold evidence of their partly alien origin (I might give them the ability to avoid doing this later). They have the ability to secrete sex pheromones to seduce other humans, a built in Mind 2, Life 3 effect. They cease aging around 30. <br /> <br /> Story-wise, I have it that they are aided by Technocracy Mages who create artificial needs in individual sleepers by destabilizing their biorhythms and brain hemisphere balance. The need for a &quot;savior&quot; of some kind is built up in the minds of the subjects so that they readily accept - intensely believe in - the Synthetics. The sleeper's life depends on it. The Synthetics have Stabilizing Resonance, which they channel through abilities and techniques to repair the sleepers.<br /> <br /> I am using Unbelief as a plot element that pushes Technomancers to conduct cruel experiments on sleepers in the name of integrating the Synthetics. The idea is that a single vital relationship becomes the foundation for integration and the Synthetic, to some degree, overcoming Unbelief. I'm looking for any phenomena described in the books that could make this story fit the rules as closely as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T06:32:29-08:00","id":1468126,"title":"","content":"Unbelief doesn't have &quot;mechanics&quot; per se. It's more of a <i>suggestion</i>, it's an element of the Setting w/o concrete rules that can end spells and things that offend the local paradigm. On the side of spells, it can be the IOC justification behind why some effects can't be made permanent (ST discretion). Creatures that look supernatural and/or have obviously supernatural skills have to seek more amenable Reality Zones, or become Thaumnivores (require to eat Quintessence to survive - ST discretion how much. The more supernatural, the more juice they need)<br /> <br /> As far as Unbelief goes, these aliens seem relatively kosher. Them being unaging and with a little too powerful atraction may justify them becoming Thaumnivores. But probably not of the kind that require <i>a lot</i> of juice to sustain themselves (they're no giant dragon). Don't know if you want them to be &quot;inmortal&quot; or just look young 'til they die of old age, if it's the former a case could be made for them to require more Quint after outliving any human<br /> <br /> An idea to &quot; fit the rules as closely as possible&quot;: Maybe they can convert (or be genetically engineered to convert) the mental energy involved in relationships (emotion and such) into Quintessence to fend off Unbelief, becoming a kind of psychic vampire","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-17-2021, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}